[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
openproject-mcp %%MCP_VER%% is installed (supergateway %%SG_VER%%).

This is a DEV-only CloudBSD port. www/openproject remains usable
without MCP. Default is disabled:

  openproject_mcp_enable=NO

Do not enable on production. Pins are global under LOCALBASE
(%%PREFIX%%/bin/openproject-mcp and %%PREFIX%%/bin/supergateway).
Runtime does not call npx.

1. Create secrets as mode 0600 (samples are placeholders):

     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/mcp.api_key.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/mcp.api_key
     # line 1: OpenProject API token (My Account → Access tokens)
     chmod 0600 %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/mcp.api_key

     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/mcp.bearer.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/mcp.bearer
     # line 1: nginx Bearer token (not the API key)
     chmod 0600 %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/mcp.bearer

2. Merge %%PREFIX%%/etc/nginx/openproject-mcp.conf.sample
   into the DEV TLS vhost (location /mcp → 127.0.0.1:8000
   with Bearer auth). Reload nginx.

3. OpenProject Puma must already listen on 127.0.0.1:3000
   (service openproject). Then:

     sysrc openproject_mcp_enable=YES
     service openproject_mcp start

HTTP:  127.0.0.1:8000/mcp (streamable HTTP via supergateway)
Stdio: %%PREFIX%%/libexec/openproject_mcp_stdio (SSH bridges)
EOM
}
]
